{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/253802-what-is-the-wyrd","id":253802,"title":"What is the Wyrd?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Changeling: The Lost"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-09-09T21:34:22-07:00","id":253802,"title":"What is the Wyrd?","content":"This question came up in another thread, and it sparked in my brain. This is mainly to start up a discussion, so I don't know if there's going to be a particularly noteworthy thesis here...<br /> <br /> So. What is the Wyrd, to me? It's a mishmash of concepts and ideas. It's Fate - the concept that what will be will be, and indeed must be. It's what Terry Pratchett might call Narrative Causality - the truth that there is a story to the world, and it tells itself every day. It's cousin to honor, half-brother to truth, and the bastard son of universal oneness and the Force after a particularly ill-considered night spent with schizophrenia and solipsism. It's how you know what your place is in the world, and how you can change that place. <br /> <br /> So, what is the Wyrd, to you?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1168-hobbitguy1420","name":"HobbitGuy1420","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1168_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"332"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-09T21:52:03-07:00","id":253827,"title":"","content":"It's not a matter of must be-not directly.<br /> <br /> The Wyrd's not a temporally linear force, and as mentioned in the other thread, it's a force of connection. Fate is suspected to be an aspect of the Wyrd because portents of fate often obey the laws of the Wyrd, in that you take a moment in time(for all intents and purposes of this discussion, an objective moment at that), and ties into things that it is like. These moments need not be direct-it's more like the outline of such, an archetype of a moment. It also doesn't have to work in that order, it can quite happily go the other way, finding the most appropriate things and tying them to a moment. It connects people through established paths-dare I say it, tropes?- and leaves the trail of breadcrumbs. It's not an active force in the way Strangers are, it doesn't pick a person to fill a role, more like people fall into its' web of winds. But the effect is the same.<br /> <br /> In this sense, the Wyrd might not be fate, but instead, and more alarmingly, Fate is merely one side of the Wyrd. And without Clarity to keep it intact, it's the main threat to changelings, because it connects them to the roles they are most ready to fit as it spins together connectivity, which propogates some very...bad ideas about self and the world for the changeling.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-09T21:54:26-07:00","id":253829,"title":"","content":"*Reads title* Kind of odd?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/490-omenseer","name":"omenseer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar490_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"987"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-10T00:11:36-07:00","id":253876,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/253802-what-is-the-wyrd?p=253827#post253827\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In this sense, the Wyrd might not be fate, but instead, and more alarmingly, Fate is merely one side of the Wyrd.</div> </div> </div> </div>So, assuming this bit is true, and I like it so I'm going to assume it's true, that raises the obvious follow-up question of &quot;What is another side of the Wyrd?&quot; I'm tempted to create an axis of Prosaic to Inspired, because of the narrator-perspective spin, but it doesn't feel like that properly plays into the Wyrd. A quick skim through the Wikipedia page suggests that Wyrd is law (and might possibly imply that to be mortal is to break said law).<br /> <br /> Nothing that really answers my question there, though. I think &quot;side&quot; might be the wrong metaphor and perhaps &quot;layer&quot; more accurate, though I couldn't say if Fate is the shallowest or deepest part of the Wyrd.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/253802-what-is-the-wyrd?p=253827#post253827\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And without Clarity to keep it intact, it's the main threat to changelings, because it connects them to the roles they are most ready to fit as it spins together connectivity, which propogates some very...bad ideas about self and the world for the changeling.</div> </div> </div> </div>Clarity being the basis of Agency? There's something. Clarity being the assertiveness of one's identity: that you helm the ship that is your life despite the storm-tossed seas. Wyrd is the wind, in that metaphor, one part the prevailing norms, one part turbulence, one part propelling force, the strength of it depending on how you angle your sail against it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I call the Integrity-analogue the &quot;<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/822559-trying-to-understand-the-morality-system?p=825008#post825008\" target=\"_blank\">subjective stat</a>&quot;.<br /> An explanation how to <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/913221-using-social-manuevering\" target=\"_blank\">use Social Manuevering</a>.<br /> Guanxi Explanations: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/787518-the-mysterium-and-their-contribution-to-mage-society?p=787824#post787824\" target=\"_blank\">1</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/787518-the-mysterium-and-their-contribution-to-mage-society?p=788173#post788173\" target=\"_blank\">2</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/833863-mages-and-trading-favors?p=834531#post834531\" target=\"_blank\">3</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2758-errol216","name":"Errol216","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1112"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-10T10:01:32-07:00","id":254161,"title":"","content":"Pretty much. Clarity is important to the assertion of one's agency and identity because it means you aren't being motivated false ideas about yourself and the world. A person who can see things as they are has more control over their choices than a person who's understanding is nothing but lies, illusion and dream.<br /> <br /> Despite my use of wind earlier, I like seeing the Wyrd as an ocean, but either is applicable(I'm not a fan of 'the Wyrd is <i>aliiiiiive</i>'). It pushes you to be something according to the convenience of connection. It makes you a prince, a beggar, a conqueror, a victim. There are times where it's tempting to let it chart your course, to take advantage of what it wants you to be.<br /> <br /> You'd only be a victim of the world, and isn't everyone already one of those?<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:8px\"><span style=\"font-size:9px\"><b>don't let it fool you</b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\">As for other aspects, law is very definitely one, at least as humanity thinks of it in terms of the basics.<br /> <br /> The problem with a ultimately connective force is that it can be a lot of things.</span></span></span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-10T12:33:41-07:00","id":254283,"title":"","content":"The way I have always seen it, the Wyrd is the Destiny that replaced the one you had lost in Arcadia.. Changelings were once people with lives and stories, which while small in comparison to a fairy lords', were still their own. That changed after their Keeper abducted them, twisting their bodies and minds to better reflect whatever grandiloquent story that the fairy lord was using as their identity. The Wyrd is to fate like a script to a play and a changeling in thrall is an unwilling actor, lacking the ability to influence the production.<br /> <br /> At some point, the changeling finds the Clarity to take control of their own narrative and escape ... but that doesn't mean that their fate is now their own. The Wyrd still rules their destiny, and a changeling's identity still bears evidence of their Durance in Arcadia. The Wyrd enforces a changeling's fairy narrative with Contracts and Blessings. Every time a changeling invokes the powers granted to him by a Contract or Blessing, they reaffirm their part in their manipulated fate ... which if followed to its logical terminus means a return to Arcadia and an end to the Clarity that allows them the ability to govern their own lives. <br /> <br /> Not everything is doom and gloom, though. If Arcadia taught the Lost anything it taught them that a person's fate is not absolute and that it can be mastered if one has the strength of will.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1996-firefly-night","name":"Firefly Night","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1996_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"150"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-11T11:17:39-07:00","id":254444,"title":"","content":"Wyrd is intangible power and a macro resource that guides/attracts Glamour in moving from place to place, place to person, etc.<br /> <br /> I'm not sure how Wyrd relates to destiny or fate or lack of sentient agency except perhaps that you can make choices that work with Wyrd or against it. No different than making choices that work with Gravity or against it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Arref</b><br /> <span style=\"color:#0000FF\"><span style=\"font-size:10px\"><i>......making magic since 1154 B.C.</i></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2062-arref","name":"Arref","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"32"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-12T12:44:42-07:00","id":255507,"title":"","content":"The Wyrd is.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/490-omenseer","name":"omenseer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar490_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"987"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-12T13:29:23-07:00","id":255541,"title":"","content":"the Wyrd may Be","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">Second Chance for<br /> <img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=709\" data-tempid=\"temp_709_1572548741915_354\" /><br /> A Beautiful Madness</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/425-seraph-kitty","name":"Seraph Kitty","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar425_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"394"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-12T21:32:12-07:00","id":255819,"title":"","content":"And shall be.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/490-omenseer","name":"omenseer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar490_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"987"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-17T15:17:58-07:00","id":259282,"title":"","content":"I regard the Wyrd as the true heart and master of Arcadia, in whatever way such a thing can be said to exist.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2244-nothri","name":"nothri","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"485"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}